+## Cancelled contracts leave active responder inquiries — 2026-10-12
+
+The owner confirmed that successful Partner Contract cancellation removes its inquiries from every active Sabalan responder list and the pending-response count, whether no rows, some rows, or all rows have already received answers. The cancelled inquiry remains accessible only as read-only history under existing access scopes; prior prices, rejection reasons and audit evidence are retained.
+
+After cancellation is successfully recorded, neither a price nor a rejection for correction may be recorded, including from a previously opened form or a direct submission. Cancellation and response submission must have a consistent ordering: an answer recorded before cancellation remains historical evidence; a submission after cancellation is rejected. Merely opening the cancellation dialog is not a completed cancellation.
+
+The same behavior applies to already-cancelled contracts with outstanding inquiry rows. An open responder list or detail page automatically refreshes to reflect cancellation; server enforcement takes effect upon successful cancellation independently of when that refresh occurs. List eligibility, pagination and counts must agree.
+
+Reactivation retains the existing requirement for fresh inquiries for every pricing subject. Old offers remain historical and must never become actionable merely because the contract is reactivated.
+
+Local implementation closes pending inquiry rows and pricing duties in the cancellation transaction, retains answered evidence, and serializes responder decisions with the owning Case lock. Read projections also enforce cancellation for legacy data and exclude inquiries from previous activation cycles. Open responder pages refresh every 15 seconds while visible and on focus, reconnection or visibility changes; pending or uncertain commands retain their exact retry payload.
+
+Local regression checks cover cancellation before pricing, partially answered pricing, already-cancelled data, queue counts and history, both cancellation/answer commit orderings, and fresh-inquiry requirements after reactivation. An existing financial-registration test fails with FORBIDDEN on both the candidate and an isolated copy of unchanged HEAD; it is not evidence of a cancellation regression. Local browser and build evidence is retained under `tmp/qa/partner-inquiry-cancellation/`. No remote Git publication or production change is authorized or implied.
+
+Focused local acceptance passed: five Case cancellation/reactivation/queue/concurrency integration scenarios, eighteen inquiry integration/concurrency tests, eighty-nine contract-package tests, responder presentation/transport tests, four browser cancellation scenarios at 1280px and 390px with light/dark accessibility checks, frontend/backend builds, database ownership and Design System checks. The final `sabalanerp-local` images were rebuilt and `npm run docker:verify` passed with all six services healthy. Browser scenarios use controlled inquiry responses; server-side cancellation and serialization are verified separately against the existing local PostgreSQL service.
+
+Accounting test follow-up on 2026-10-12 resolved the previously recorded financial-registration failure. The old fixture supplied explicit Partner ACCOUNTING_READ/ACCOUNTING_WRITE grants but omitted the Accounting workspace and the exact `accounting_invoice_candidates_manage` operation required by ADR-0123. Preparation correctly succeeded while queueing correctly returned FORBIDDEN. The fixture now supplies Accounting workspace edit and invoice-operation edit without changing runtime authorization. The regression additionally verifies rejection with broad grants alone or workspace edit alone, no financial/reporting effect on rejection, live operation revocation even for an existing queue receipt, and idempotent registration after permission restoration.
+
+Follow-up validation passed all 58 tests across Case draft/lifecycle, inquiry integration/concurrency and Accounting permission-bridge suites, plus the backend build, database ownership check and diff whitespace check. All database tests used the existing local PostgreSQL service with rollback or the repository's isolated-schema database harness and cleanup. This follow-up changes test data and coverage only; no production permissions or runtime authorization rules changed.
+
