+
+## Automatic Partner inquiry presentation — design interview, 2026-10-12
+
+The owner confirmed automatic presentation updates in both the Partner Contract detail and the Partner Contract list when Sabalan records an inquiry response. A delay of 15–30 seconds is acceptable for an active page. Update the displayed status and inquiry-review action while preserving unsaved user input; do not automatically open the response or show an additional arrival notification.
+
+The owner explicitly rejected exposing the Partner inquiry-review action for partial responses: keep it hidden until Sabalan has completely answered the Contract's current inquiry. Stop periodic checks while the tab is hidden and obtain fresh state on return. Keep list filters, counts and rows consistent when a response changes eligibility; a Contract leaving the active list filter does not automatically close its already-open detail page.
+
+The owner confirmed that a completely answered current inquiry containing rejected rows exposes the review action and displays the main Contract label `استعلام شده`. Once the Partner corrects and resubmits the rejected items to Sabalan, the Contract displays `در انتظار استعلام` again. This explicitly supersedes the 2026-10-03 display rule excluding rejected offers from `استعلام شده`; it does not change price acceptance or commercial finality.
+
+When automatic reads fail, preserve existing information and unsaved input, show a small stale-state message with a manual retry action, and increase the interval between automatic retries. The server must revalidate current state and authority before recording an action.
+
+The owner also confirmed that expiry of quoted prices does not undo the completely answered inquiry's `استعلام شده` presentation. Show price expiry in the review surface and prohibit accepting expired prices; display `در انتظار استعلام` only after successfully submitting a new inquiry. Contract expiry remains distinct and takes precedence over this inquiry presentation. This supersedes the prior exclusion of expired offers from the complete-response display rule without extending price validity.
+
+The owner approved lightweight change checks every 20 seconds while the page is visible, rather than repeated full Contract reads. Fetch the required updated information only when a change is detected; coalesce simultaneous refresh requests, preserve input and page position, pause periodic checks in hidden tabs and reduce retry frequency after failures. Reads must use current authorization and must not serve stale status or pricing from a cache. Measure request volume and database-query cost during acceptance; this design decision does not establish achieved load reduction or a strict refresh deadline under network failure.
+
+Implementation and validation of this Partner-side automatic refresh remain pending. The confirmed complete-response gate will narrow the current review-action eligibility.
