+The owner confirmed the shared design and authorized implementation. The owner also requested removal of automatic refresh specifically from the Sabalan responder's inquiry list. That list retains its manual refresh and normal reads when navigating or changing filters; this supersedes the earlier automatic responder-list refresh requirement. The responder detail refresh and server-side cancellation enforcement remain in scope of their existing rules.
+
+## Customer acceptance boundary during repeated wholesale negotiations — 2026-10-12
+
+The owner confirmed that any actual change to the customer-facing products, delivery plan or payment plan requires fresh Customer acceptance for the changed agreement. Repeated rejection, re-offer and acceptance of Sabalan-to-Partner wholesale pricing alone must preserve Customer acceptance when the Partner-to-Customer agreement is unchanged, including the second and subsequent negotiation rounds. The number of wholesale negotiation rounds is not an acceptance-reset condition.
+
+This exception does not cover product changes made to resolve an inquiry rejection: those remain customer-facing agreement changes and require new acceptance. Prior acceptance remains historical evidence rather than acceptance of changed terms. Wholesale negotiation history and price-validity/finality checks remain intact. The runtime paths are being reviewed against this confirmed boundary; this documentation does not establish implemented or tested behavior.
+
+The owner clarified that "product change" covers any actual change to the saved information in the Product Selection step, not merely replacement, addition or removal of a product. Preserve this full step boundary when detecting changes that require renewed Customer acceptance. Merely opening the step without changing its saved information does not create a changed agreement. Wholesale-only negotiation remains separate from changes to Product Selection information.
+
+The owner confirmed that wholesale-only preservation of Customer acceptance also applies to authorized corrections of previously final Contracts, provided the Customer agreement remains unchanged. Existing Accounting permission, financial correction, audit and finality gates continue to apply; retaining Customer acceptance does not authorize an otherwise forbidden price change.
+
+The owner clarified that the payment-plan reset boundary is the Customer-to-Partner payment plan. Changes only to the Partner-to-Sabalan payment terms are independent and do not require new Customer acceptance when Product Selection information, the Customer delivery plan and the Customer payment plan remain unchanged.
+
+The owner rejected displaying the waiting/answered inquiry label in place of the edit reset: any actual saved Contract edit returns the Contract to `یادداشت`. This is distinct from the previously confirmed wholesale-only negotiation flow. The owner explicitly confirmed that the post-edit Contract remains `یادداشت` until the Partner Seller confirms the edited Contract again, even if Sabalan has completely answered the current inquiry. Inquiry response arrival alone must not clear this post-edit note gate; Customer acceptance also must not substitute for the required Partner confirmation. After Partner confirmation, apply the current inquiry presentation with cancellation, Contract expiry and valid finality retaining their existing precedence. Renewed Customer acceptance continues to follow the Customer-agreement boundary above.
+
+## Local automatic inquiry presentation acceptance — 2026-10-12
+
+The Sabalan responder list now has manual refresh only; its normal navigation/filter reads remain. Partner list and detail surfaces use owner-authorized, private/no-store change-version checks every 20 seconds while visible. Fingerprints cover Case and inquiry-row revisions, contract updates, time-dependent expiry, authority and Profile lifecycle. Unchanged checks do not fetch full Case projections. Changed reads preserve the displayed list, search, page position and entered form values, and omit supplementary collection/correction reloads during background inquiry updates. Hidden tabs stop scheduling; returning online or visible checks immediately, simultaneous automatic triggers share one in-flight check, and failed checks back off to a maximum of two minutes with a retry action.
+
+Current-request completion is separate from usable pricing: partial responses remain unavailable for review, while complete responses including rejected or expired offers can be reviewed. Pending successor requests remove completion even when old valid pricing evidence remains reusable. Post-edit note precedence requires renewed Partner approval independently of Customer acceptance. Actual Product Selection/customer-agreement changes reset acceptance; wholesale-only authorized corrections retain the accepted Customer evidence with explicit revision-lineage audit and do not relax Accounting or finality controls.
+
+Local evidence: 40 Case Draft/database integration scenarios passed, plus the change-version HTTP test covering strict input, no-store response, current Profile lifecycle and actor deactivation; two inquiry-completion regressions passed; 90 shared-contract tests and 23 frontend case/list/view tests passed. Five browser scenarios passed, covering unchanged checks without full reloads, a visible table during a held changed read, preserved search and entered reason, hidden-tab pause, concurrent-trigger coalescing, failure backoff/recovery, manual responder-list refresh at 1280px/390px, and retained responder-detail cancellation enforcement. Browser inquiry data is controlled; backend behavior is exercised separately against isolated transactions in the existing local PostgreSQL service.
